[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-337105"] :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}).\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ then general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\ny(t)=(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-t+C}{(1-t)^{2}})f(t)+g(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find $f(t)+g(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1}=\\frac{1}{t(1-t)}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1}=\\frac{1}{t(1-t)}\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2/(t-1)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t-1|} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =(t-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(t-1)^{2}\\frac{2x}{t-1}=(t-1)^{2}\\frac{1}{t(1-t)} \\\\ (t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(t-1)x=-(t-1)^{2}\\frac{1}{t(t-1)} \\\\ (t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(t-1)x=-\\frac{t-1}{t} \\\\ (t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(t-1)x=\\frac{1-t}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2}) & =\\frac{1-t}{t} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\frac{1-t}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =\\int \\frac{1}{t}-1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-t+C \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-t+C}{(t-1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-t+C}{(t-1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo recover $y$, we substitute $x$ into\n\n$$\ny=x{t}^{2}+t,\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-t+C}{(t-1)^{2}}){t}^{2}+t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $f(t)={t}^{2},g(t)=t,$ and\n\n$$\nf(t)+g(t)={t}^{2}+t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-337654/selection/35498b6fda030a4eddd1ccbbe51e22c1da6eea715e4aa1913bc1dd6f8b3e9540" :answer/id #uuid "a09f4695-87c0-5c59-99a3-e27d7bdf5ec9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=12+4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337654/selection/99557f5bdba256d0ecc685dc05fa398add0c92ab71b5b4aac85f190c54c61af3" :answer/id #uuid "09329e11-f928-5aaa-a6a0-bb64530cfe3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=9-4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337654/selection/e5cb8608893a1d7f87ed9d86b9a0f61851f9aedad62d59bc3270ee110f428cdf" :answer/id #uuid "05db37f1-42d3-5c07-bb56-b7d101ef6064" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=12-2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337654/selection/57f56e9de9f998cc9b1cb3171a4370cccac9d281b039eac11cf52a0ca8e4e6d8" :answer/id #uuid "5fd596b3-3a69-5f6f-bc6c-b6921485bd2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=12-4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337654/selection/4ff2bf1ce6dcf2a0e6ed0ba19434a011f2160d6c8c0a2d0b60b124412b4366f4" :answer/id #uuid "387a3d7d-f0d8-5fdf-a188-04d35defaf8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=4-12t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337654/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "88b6c6e7-636e-5fa6-b403-c5a3a19a0818" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337654/selection/57f56e9de9f998cc9b1cb3171a4370cccac9d281b039eac11cf52a0ca8e4e6d8" :answer-field/choices ["q-337654/selection/35498b6fda030a4eddd1ccbbe51e22c1da6eea715e4aa1913bc1dd6f8b3e9540" "q-337654/selection/99557f5bdba256d0ecc685dc05fa398add0c92ab71b5b4aac85f190c54c61af3" "q-337654/selection/e5cb8608893a1d7f87ed9d86b9a0f61851f9aedad62d59bc3270ee110f428cdf" "q-337654/selection/57f56e9de9f998cc9b1cb3171a4370cccac9d281b039eac11cf52a0ca8e4e6d8" "q-337654/selection/4ff2bf1ce6dcf2a0e6ed0ba19434a011f2160d6c8c0a2d0b60b124412b4366f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337654" :question/id #uuid "3f42ef78-77b3-5413-802e-b393932da492" :question/math-academy-id "q-337654" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x(3+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})+2{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ then general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\nx(t)=C{e}^{-t/3}+f(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find the function $f(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{1}{3}x=-\\frac{4}{3}t.\n$$\n\n*You may also wish to make use of the following result (constants omitted):*\n\n$$\n\\int t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t=(t-1){e}^{t}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{1}{3}x=-\\frac{4}{3}t.\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t),\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t}={e}^{\\int \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}t}={e}^{t/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t/3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{1}{3}x{e}^{t/3} & =-\\frac{4}{3}t{e}^{t/3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{t/3}) & =-\\frac{4}{3}t{e}^{t/3} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{t/3})\\,\\text{d}t & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\int t{e}^{t/3}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the integral, let $u=\\frac{t}{3}.$ Then $t=3u$ and $\\text{d}t=3\\,\\text{d}u,$ so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int t{e}^{t/3}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int (3u){e}^{u}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =9\\int u{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =9(u-1){e}^{u}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting back $u=\\frac{t}{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int t{e}^{t/3}\\,\\text{d}t & =9(\\frac{t}{3}-1){e}^{t/3} \\\\  & =(3t-9){e}^{t/3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{t/3} & =-\\frac{4}{3}(3t-9){e}^{t/3}+C \\\\  & =(-4t+12){e}^{t/3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\nx=-4t+12+C{e}^{-t/3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\nx(t)=C{e}^{-t/3}+12-4t\n$$\n\nand finally, $f(t)=12-4t.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337654/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6bb3f2e-ee56-56f2-94f2-4b454a187ab7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337654"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337850/selection/c7b50867c579be6174f9c0f8800a310624b0ed315f56ed440a0980c61bfda22f" :answer/id #uuid "9bf805d4-81bd-5a66-8284-b6298da82573" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{t}^{2}-t-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337850/selection/6506162df43587b0dfc88f547287f5a7599492d90337760b5b2733f73f8947a9" :answer/id #uuid "6872f006-57d3-5b87-ac29-7b4e2e40b21a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{t}^{2}+t-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337850/selection/58a96852419e790293d86a3bb69caa1d52831daab11b8b33b33ed5bba719e16c" :answer/id #uuid "bd5349ef-ab8b-5b64-b1c5-a734c15eac7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{t}^{2}+t+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337850/selection/74dd78afd6bff79fd7d777b49d5b81d2433d59c9023bfa064cdeda2c65df4bc0" :answer/id #uuid "45b6ea67-9d1d-5db0-a578-d047204f9fd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{t}^{2}+t-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337850/selection/6c3aca771034dca9a8219057b763432548444accbdae128fb572203a08a114ca" :answer/id #uuid "ebcda567-04a9-5e13-b5b3-4550b06adfc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{t}^{2}+t-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337850/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "98880f9b-7288-54cb-b393-8a8764e9b39f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337850/selection/74dd78afd6bff79fd7d777b49d5b81d2433d59c9023bfa064cdeda2c65df4bc0" :answer-field/choices ["q-337850/selection/c7b50867c579be6174f9c0f8800a310624b0ed315f56ed440a0980c61bfda22f" "q-337850/selection/6506162df43587b0dfc88f547287f5a7599492d90337760b5b2733f73f8947a9" "q-337850/selection/58a96852419e790293d86a3bb69caa1d52831daab11b8b33b33ed5bba719e16c" "q-337850/selection/74dd78afd6bff79fd7d777b49d5b81d2433d59c9023bfa064cdeda2c65df4bc0" "q-337850/selection/6c3aca771034dca9a8219057b763432548444accbdae128fb572203a08a114ca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337850" :question/id #uuid "84fc93c7-80a7-5e68-b1f8-c5227f556ef8" :question/math-academy-id "q-337850" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3)+2{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ then general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\ny(t)=(C{e}^{t/3}-4t-12)f(t)+g(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find $f(t)+g(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{1}{3}x=\\frac{4}{3}t.\n$$\n\n*You may also wish to make use of the following result (constants omitted):*\n\n$$\n\\int t{e}^{-t/3}\\,\\text{d}t=(-3t-9){e}^{-t/3}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{1}{3}x=\\frac{4}{3}t.\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-t/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t/3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{1}{3}x{e}^{-t/3} & =\\frac{4}{3}t{e}^{-t/3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{-t/3}) & =\\frac{4}{3}t{e}^{-t/3} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{-t/3})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{4}{3}\\int t{e}^{-t/3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x{e}^{-t/3} & =\\frac{4}{3}(-3t-9){e}^{-t/3}+C \\\\ x & =-4t-12+C{e}^{t/3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\nx(t)=C{e}^{t/3}-4t-12.\n$$\n\nTo recover $y$, we substitute $x$ into\n\n$$\ny=x(t-3)+2{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =(C{e}^{t/3}-4t-12)(t-3)+2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $f(t)=t-3,\\text{ }g(t)=2{t}^{2},$ and\n\n$$\nf(t)+g(t)=2{t}^{2}+t-3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-337850/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6bb3f2e-ee56-56f2-94f2-4b454a187ab7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337850"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365372/field-1/be1274b5937c367216245688342c0e86021f5daec7130ebeea0d962ae6d17243" :answer/id #uuid "e3c1b8d5-a84c-515a-a9ed-6a8abf2aec2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{t-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365372/field-1/1c4c628cb6d3569984b004088e5e22f94472fc0e886c939f1771842a7dc6c631" :answer/id #uuid "f3a3fab5-e427-5224-8ae4-cf9255d02671" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365372/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" :answer/id #uuid "4276ec8e-9b01-5466-9efe-dc1e655463f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365372/field-1/6b5a3a25e7a7bac75948e98b4b4715e94fde5a111a3d6a494d4d66066f7e87f7" :answer/id #uuid "94fd8747-fd34-5774-902b-b69b91156e3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t(t-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365372/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3a7fbc8-7b63-5b5f-a8c7-291512e0531d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365372/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-365372/field-1/be1274b5937c367216245688342c0e86021f5daec7130ebeea0d962ae6d17243" "q-365372/field-1/1c4c628cb6d3569984b004088e5e22f94472fc0e886c939f1771842a7dc6c631" "q-365372/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" "q-365372/field-1/6b5a3a25e7a7bac75948e98b4b4715e94fde5a111a3d6a494d4d66066f7e87f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365372/field-2/1cefbdc64370ed55a90b5cf2ede144358f69d2ed177dc8aaa3af711d5e936c74" :answer/id #uuid "95040dc4-beec-562f-a766-89d2b28bc5c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t(1-t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365372/field-2/c0ca61c0bd838d60ab84e49882f4eb2c3638c9fb0daf529e53b977224679f9b3" :answer/id #uuid "2af022b1-baa8-53d7-979a-8de2cf0b7d96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{t(1-t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365372/field-2/e78a7e5bb010abd9884bb0c098584cd7702f6355575b54142808414644dff241" :answer/id #uuid "dba1a800-0b1b-5cc9-adad-740edce9e56e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{t(3-t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365372/field-2/e7fad66861ae18bdde594f409bcb6a8f18f4234423867f5c5e7d05aaa6c546f0" :answer/id #uuid "32c6d1d1-3ce1-5a2c-b8ee-3649988b03d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365372/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "00c1a548-3cbc-547e-abc4-ddce42e5615a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365372/field-2/c0ca61c0bd838d60ab84e49882f4eb2c3638c9fb0daf529e53b977224679f9b3" :answer-field/choices ["q-365372/field-2/1cefbdc64370ed55a90b5cf2ede144358f69d2ed177dc8aaa3af711d5e936c74" "q-365372/field-2/c0ca61c0bd838d60ab84e49882f4eb2c3638c9fb0daf529e53b977224679f9b3" "q-365372/field-2/e78a7e5bb010abd9884bb0c098584cd7702f6355575b54142808414644dff241" "q-365372/field-2/e7fad66861ae18bdde594f409bcb6a8f18f4234423867f5c5e7d05aaa6c546f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365372" :question/id #uuid "f1849fca-686f-575a-b1ad-f816fd7436dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-365372" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation, defined for $t>0:$\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nUsing the substitution $t=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ the equation can be transformed to a first-order linear equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the functions $P$ and $Q.$\n\n$\\,\\,P(t)=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,Q(t)=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nIn our case, we wish to transform the equation\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\ninto a first-order linear equation for $x=x(t).$ We proceed in three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Substitute, and differentiate with respect to $x.$\n\nWe have the substitution\n\n$$\nt=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=x{t}^{2}+3t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating both sides with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x{t}^{2}+3t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum and product rules and using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x{t}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3t) \\\\ t & ={t}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({t}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3t) \\\\ t & ={t}^{2}+2xt\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+3\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Isolate the derivative and take its reciprocal.\n\nWe isolate $\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-{t}^{2} & =2xt\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+3\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ t(1-t) & =(2xt+3)\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{t(1-t)}{2xt+3} & =\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{t(1-t)}{2xt+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by taking the reciprocal of each side, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{2xt+3}{t(1-t)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Express the derivative as a first-order linear equation.\n\nFinally, we write this in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{2xt+3}{t(1-t)} \\\\ t(1-t)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =2xt+3 \\\\ t(1-t)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-2xt & =3 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{2xt}{t(1-t)} & =\\frac{3}{t(1-t)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{2x}{1-t} & =\\frac{3}{t(1-t)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1} & =\\frac{3}{t(1-t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{2}{t-1},\\,Q(t)=\\frac{3}{t(1-t)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-365372/field-1" "q-365372/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126ffd6c-f5a9-564f-935f-398a126d2cbd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365372"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365378/field-1/1ff5f44098b4926bcaf9653220f009a54491cdd8792aa3552a99ea0a43512677" :answer/id #uuid "097d1c81-031e-5483-a494-5ec1ff91bc6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365378/field-1/66c9a43052c67ef0cee15e63ea59cf4f609ed05d7b7de703f51f5f20c4c96086" :answer/id #uuid "35d737a0-2ff6-5a6b-9555-6d01894fee9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365378/field-1/dd37e628956d9e28d28f5dc0915bacf53c5f0bad20b597f00769e5acad9acb48" :answer/id #uuid "cac7bc78-1ba9-585e-bf1c-69e7a8e0103f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}{t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365378/field-1/254ec71ee9cdf246e6933a953b2d0d4d3f33a6e30c43be4dd5cf81db21933f8d" :answer/id #uuid "51a0ec5e-7033-504f-a1a2-e6a320ffe381" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365378/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a0c16fc-4dde-5203-aae7-d3e06c20598e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365378/field-1/1ff5f44098b4926bcaf9653220f009a54491cdd8792aa3552a99ea0a43512677" :answer-field/choices ["q-365378/field-1/1ff5f44098b4926bcaf9653220f009a54491cdd8792aa3552a99ea0a43512677" "q-365378/field-1/66c9a43052c67ef0cee15e63ea59cf4f609ed05d7b7de703f51f5f20c4c96086" "q-365378/field-1/dd37e628956d9e28d28f5dc0915bacf53c5f0bad20b597f00769e5acad9acb48" "q-365378/field-1/254ec71ee9cdf246e6933a953b2d0d4d3f33a6e30c43be4dd5cf81db21933f8d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365378/field-2/fdcaf63b034f232008db5d48dae4a55433636c486d19e7247c2caa5455fef011" :answer/id #uuid "9cd9eb53-fbcf-5d70-832e-abdd06620e3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365378/field-2/88866a327f433b60419ca397868b51927f76782a7ef45d004c737bcf83b981e8" :answer/id #uuid "3115e29d-ace3-5656-8349-8d2c7a65732c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365378/field-2/2cb0343bbc75a35335a394e163d791184ad12c5d63769e7fd806802fffa4b87d" :answer/id #uuid "4e2162a8-3912-5152-8c6e-6b82e40d2d9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-3}{t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365378/field-2/2892be3f9869fd6dbe3720b48eb33c7fb883b802f9bc11e6cc207257c649b092" :answer/id #uuid "9a7a1c17-11a7-5444-bbd6-8f5b656216a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365378/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3224547-1380-56fd-9675-9539b59f3109" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365378/field-2/2892be3f9869fd6dbe3720b48eb33c7fb883b802f9bc11e6cc207257c649b092" :answer-field/choices ["q-365378/field-2/fdcaf63b034f232008db5d48dae4a55433636c486d19e7247c2caa5455fef011" "q-365378/field-2/88866a327f433b60419ca397868b51927f76782a7ef45d004c737bcf83b981e8" "q-365378/field-2/2cb0343bbc75a35335a394e163d791184ad12c5d63769e7fd806802fffa4b87d" "q-365378/field-2/2892be3f9869fd6dbe3720b48eb33c7fb883b802f9bc11e6cc207257c649b092"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365378" :question/id #uuid "e710fdcc-e8a9-51c3-80b2-82b2d67b13ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-365378" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=xcos\\,(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})-3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the substitution $t=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ the equation can be transformed to a first-order linear equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the functions $P$ and $Q.$\n\n$\\,\\,P(t)=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,Q(t)=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nIn our case, we wish to transform the equation\n\n$$\ny=xcos\\,(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})-3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\ninto a first-order linear equation for $x=x(t).$ We proceed in three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Substitute, and differentiate with respect to $x.$\n\nWe have the substitution\n\n$$\nt=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-3t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating both sides with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-3t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum and product rules and using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3t) \\\\ t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3t) \\\\ t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}-3\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Isolate the derivative and take its reciprocal.\n\nWe isolate $\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & =-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}-3\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & =-(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+3)\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ -\\frac{t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+3} & =\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t}{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by taking the reciprocal of each side, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+3}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Express the derivative as a first-order linear equation.\n\nFinally, we write this in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+3}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t} \\\\ (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+3 \\\\ (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & =3 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t} & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)} & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)},\\,Q(t)=\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-365378/field-1" "q-365378/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126ffd6c-f5a9-564f-935f-398a126d2cbd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365378"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
